1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,040
Hi, I'm Tom from the Burp Scanner development team. Today I'm going to talk a little bit about

2
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:11,160
recorded login sequences. So recorded login sequences are kind of our one-size-fits-all

3
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:14,120
solution for the many different ways of authenticating that are out there on the

4
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:18,780
modern web. Burp Scanner out-of-the-box will handle really simple login forms that just have

5
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:22,920
a username and a password field, but those aren't too prevalent these days. So instead,

6
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:28,140
recorded login sequences enable you to handle any arbitrary logins that are out there, rather than

7
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:33,960
having us try to support everything out of the box and always playing catch-up. We can just handle

8
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:38,160
anything that can be recorded and replayed. So I'm going to dive into Burp and I'm going to show you

9
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:42,340
how to record one, how to replay it, to check that it's working. And if I remember, because this is

10
